## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, beginner-friendly design for tenant isolation and latency without overengineering.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant read routing
- Replica lag awareness and failover
- Data isolation via schemas or tenant filters
- Caching for hot tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing logic
const hotTenants = new Set(["t1","t2"]);
function route(tenantId){
  if(hotTenants.has(tenantId)) return `reader-${tenantId}.example`;
  return 'reader-default';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate latency during a failover?
- How would you handle a sudden surge from a previously cold tenant?

